WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.240
FedRAMP evidence and documentation connect security claims to real system implementation,

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:12.420
operations, assessment, monitoring, findings, remediation, and risk decisions.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:16.160
They help stakeholders understand what the cloud service offering is,

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:20.300
how controls are implemented, what evidence supports those controls,

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.080
what weaknesses remain, and whether security posture is being maintained over time.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:30.900
Strong documentation is scoped, consistent, current, specific, evidence-backed,

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.840
and aligned to the actual cloud service offering.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:38.620
It describes the real boundary, dependencies, shared responsibilities,

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.160
control implementations, procedures, and operational processes.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:46.820
It avoids generic promises, unsupported statements,

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.640
and idealized descriptions that do not match the live system.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:53.580
Consistency across documents is essential.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:58.200
Strong evidence is traceable, relevant, reviewable, protected,

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:03.140
and connected to control assertions, findings, remediation, and monitoring.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:07.840
It has an owner, context, date, source, and purpose.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:12.060
It supports a specific claim rather than floating as an unexplained artifact.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:17.160
It is managed carefully because it may contain sensitive security, architecture,

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:20.260
vulnerability, or operational information.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.800
The goal is not documentation volume.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:26.780
More documents do not automatically mean better security.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.640
The goal is trustworthy evidence that helps stakeholders understand whether controls are

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.820
implemented and operating as described.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:40.240
When evidence and documentation are accurate, current, and connected to action,

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:44.380
they become practical decision support for assessment, authorization support,

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:49.240
continuous monitoring, customer reuse, and risk-informed operations.
